White's Reality Check: best excess = 0.1122% per 5 days, p = 0.1494

============================================================================
VERDICT
============================================================================ 
No strategy beats the always_long baseline once data snooping is accounted for.
The best of 3 strategies produced 0.1122% excess return per 5-day period,
and the Reality Check p-value is 0.149 against a 0.05 threshold. With about
348 independent observations and overlapping returns, a result this size is
what testing 3 ideas on one history of one market produces by chance.

Unadjusted significance would have passed: none
After Benjamini-Hochberg: none

